    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0383" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1515</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-27T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 27, 1915, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.50 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Foreign Minister informs me Swedish Government now discussing with British
                    Government following three propositions regarding <pb facs="0384" n="126"
                        xml:id="pg126"/> treatment of neutral shipping: (1) convoy, (2)
                    establishment of neutral zone in North Sea, (3) setting aside of port in England
                    for use of neutral shipping only Foreign Minister adds he personally favors
                    third proposition.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
